I want to setup a benchmark repository for PyLops. It should follow a similar pattern to https://github.com/deepinv/benchmarks and use BenchOpt (https://benchopt.github.io/stable/index.html#) as the mechanisms to run the benchmarks.

Each benchmark is a PyLops problem defined by a true model, an operator, and the associated modelled data (plus possibly some noise). Different combinations of solvers and regularizers/preconditioners and then run and a set of metrics is computed on the true sol vs estimate. For the metric always use pylops MAE and PSNR.

To start I want you to scaffold the repo and use the example in SeismicInterpolation.ipynb as the first use case with 3 inversion types to compare (will add more inversion types and examples later).

I also want you to propose a setup such that these benchmarks run on a CI and store results in csv tables in the repo so they can be picked up by a post-processing script that creates a simple website.



Changes from the plan
- LSQR solver: regularized_inversion(engine="pylops") actually runs CGLS, not LSQR. The solver therefore sets up the regularised system itself (VStack([Op, epsR*D2])) and calls PyLops' lsqr.
- f-k solver: I build it as Op @ Real @ FFT2D.H. That reuses the dataset's real operator as it is and gives the same result as the library's version.
